01:09:10,558 --> 01:09:12,256
Okay, yeah,
no, I am, um...

1471
01:09:13,431 --> 01:09:15,911
I'm meeting somebody
from the Eye.

1472
01:09:15,955 --> 01:09:17,304
Yeah, no, they agreed
to meet me

1473
01:09:17,348 --> 01:09:20,264
to exchange
this computer chip
for our lives back.

1474
01:09:20,307 --> 01:09:21,787
So that's what
it's come to now.

1475
01:09:21,830 --> 01:09:23,484
I hope you're happy
with the situation
you've put us in.

1476
01:09:23,528 --> 01:09:25,094
You're talking
to the Eye?

1477
01:09:25,138 --> 01:09:26,226
Yeah.

1478
01:09:26,270 --> 01:09:28,141
Why are you talking
to the Eye?

1479
01:09:29,142 --> 01:09:30,578
Atlas.

1480
01:09:30,622 --> 01:09:32,101
Atlas,
give me the stick.

1481
01:09:32,145 --> 01:09:34,495
Dylan, you're not our
leader anymore, okay?

1482
01:09:34,539 --> 01:09:35,931
You're not our hero.

1483
01:09:35,975 --> 01:09:37,237
You're not FBI.

1484
01:09:37,281 --> 01:09:38,673
You're not
a magician.

1485
01:09:38,717 --> 01:09:40,240
You're not
really anything.

1486
01:09:40,284 --> 01:09:43,112
And we trusted you
for a year.

1487
01:09:43,156 --> 01:09:45,680
So if you really
wanna help us...
[CLEARS THROAT]

1488
01:09:45,724 --> 01:09:48,335
If you really
wanna help us,
you would leave.

1489
01:09:49,554 --> 01:09:50,903
[SCOFFS]

1490
01:09:56,778 --> 01:09:58,954
I get it. Cool.

1491
01:09:58,998 --> 01:09:59,999
Bye.

1492
01:10:17,756 --> 01:10:19,061
Hello, hello!

1493
01:10:19,105 --> 01:10:21,325
Yeah, that was me you called
at the magic shop.

1494
01:10:22,326 --> 01:10:23,936
So much fun though,

1495
01:10:23,979 --> 01:10:25,329
knowing you'd
be scurrying away
from me at the lab

1496
01:10:25,372 --> 01:10:26,721
just to bring it
to me here.

1497
01:10:26,765 --> 01:10:28,549
Did you actually
think I'd let you go?

1498
01:10:28,593 --> 01:10:29,811
How did you do that?

1499
01:10:29,855 --> 01:10:31,291
Everyone has their button.

1500
01:10:31,335 --> 01:10:32,814
You push it
and they go blind.

1501
01:10:32,858 --> 01:10:34,860
And yours,
obviously, is ego.

1502
01:10:35,600 --> 01:10:36,992
"Stay the course.

1503
01:10:37,036 --> 01:10:39,821
"Great changes
are in store.

1504
01:10:39,865 --> 01:10:42,389
"Trust that
your unique talents

1505
01:10:42,433 --> 01:10:44,043
"will not go
unrecognized."

1506
01:10:45,305 --> 01:10:46,785
That was you.Yeah.

1507
01:10:46,828 --> 01:10:48,308
Merritt downloaded
all the files,

1508
01:10:48,352 --> 01:10:51,180
but how do you think
we were able to find him?

1509
01:10:51,224 --> 01:10:52,356
Your phone.

1510
01:10:54,227 --> 01:10:56,273
I asked to see the face
behind all of this.

1511
01:10:56,316 --> 01:10:59,145
What you actually
put your phone on
was a bi-wave siphon pad.

1512
01:11:00,886 --> 01:11:03,018
Once again,

1513
01:11:03,062 --> 01:11:05,499
science beats magic.

1514
01:11:05,543 --> 01:11:07,893
So, the stick?No.

1515
01:11:08,937 --> 01:11:10,156
[GROANING]

1516
01:11:10,983 --> 01:11:12,027
I got it!

1517
01:11:12,071 --> 01:11:13,464
I got it. I got it.

1518
01:11:15,509 --> 01:11:17,424
Fuck, Dylan!Wait, leave them!

1519
01:11:17,468 --> 01:11:19,034
You really think
I'm gonna walk away
from you?

1520
01:11:19,078 --> 01:11:21,210
Give me the stick![GROANS]

1521
01:11:21,254 --> 01:11:22,429
Give me it!

1522
01:11:22,473 --> 01:11:24,301
All right. Don't ever
question me again.

1523
01:11:24,344 --> 01:11:25,302
Beat it!

1524
01:11:27,086 --> 01:11:28,653
[POUNDING ON DOOR]

1525
01:11:36,661 --> 01:11:38,750
So, the stick.Go to hell.

1526
01:11:39,577 --> 01:11:40,578
[SCOFFS] Boys.

1527
01:11:40,621 --> 01:11:42,188
[PANICKED SHOUTING]

1528
01:11:46,540 --> 01:11:47,628
[GRUNTING]

1529
01:11:53,025 --> 01:11:54,983
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

1530
01:11:55,027 --> 01:11:56,115
[GROANS]

1531
01:12:11,217 --> 01:12:12,653
WALTER:
There's like 10 of you.

1532
01:12:12,697 --> 01:12:14,525
Come on,
he's just doing tricks.

1533
01:12:14,568 --> 01:12:16,440
He's there!Go!

1534
01:12:44,032 --> 01:12:45,860
[RABBIT SQUEAKS][CROWD LAUGHING]

1535
01:12:46,644 --> 01:12:47,775
[YELPS]

1536
01:13:05,140 --> 01:13:06,228
Oh...

1537
01:13:19,633 --> 01:13:21,026
[LAUGHS]

1538
01:13:37,738 --> 01:13:40,001
[GROANING]

1539
01:13:40,045 --> 01:13:44,049
Dylan, watch
the pretty birdies fly.
And sleep.

1540
01:13:45,224 --> 01:13:46,312
Doesn't work on me.

1541
01:13:46,355 --> 01:13:48,532
Not even
as a distraction?

1542
01:13:48,575 --> 01:13:49,707
[METAL CLANKS][GROANS]

1543
01:13:51,230 --> 01:13:53,841
Good job.Nice to be involved.

1544
01:13:53,885 --> 01:13:54,929
[CHASE CHUCKLES]

1545
01:14:02,067 --> 01:14:04,156
Hey, guys! Guys! Hey!

1546
01:14:04,199 --> 01:14:05,679
I just saw Dylan.
Um, something happened.

1547
01:14:05,723 --> 01:14:06,854
What do you mean
you just saw Dylan?

1548
01:14:06,898 --> 01:14:08,943
Dylan's here?
What happened?

1549
01:14:08,987 --> 01:14:11,468
Atlas.[STAMMERS]
I don't know.

1550
01:14:16,342 --> 01:14:17,517
JACK: What are they doing?

1551
01:14:17,561 --> 01:14:20,041
ATLAS:
Those are Walter's men.

1552
01:14:20,085 --> 01:14:23,218
This is what they want.
[SIGHS]

1553
01:14:23,262 --> 01:14:25,525
What the hell?
How do you
still have that?

1554
01:14:25,569 --> 01:14:27,135
[MACHINE WHIRRING]

1555
01:14:30,443 --> 01:14:32,227
Whoa. That's
Lionel Shrike's safe.

1556
01:14:32,271 --> 01:14:34,795
What the hell
do they want with that?

1557
01:14:34,839 --> 01:14:36,623
Okay, we gotta
follow that truck.

1558
01:14:36,667 --> 01:14:40,018
ATLAS: They must have Dylan.
We don't have much time.

1559
01:14:42,455 --> 01:14:44,413
[DYLAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

1560
01:14:44,457 --> 01:14:45,719
DYLAN: What do you want?

1561
01:14:45,763 --> 01:14:49,462
You to understand something
very important.

1562
01:14:50,463 --> 01:14:51,986
We

1563
01:14:52,030 --> 01:14:53,727
are mirror images.

1564
01:14:53,771 --> 01:14:55,163
You see, because like you,

1565
01:14:55,207 --> 01:14:57,470
I share
a very deep connection
with my father.

1566
01:14:58,819 --> 01:15:01,430
And like you,
I'll stop at nothing

1567
01:15:01,474 --> 01:15:03,781
to avenge any wrongs
done to him.

1568
01:15:03,824 --> 01:15:05,783
[PUNCHING][DYLAN GROANS]

1569
01:15:08,437 --> 01:15:12,006
You know the only difference
between your father and mine?

1570
01:15:12,050 --> 01:15:13,921
Mine's still alive.

1571
01:15:14,618 --> 01:15:15,793
Get him up.

1572
01:15:29,328 --> 01:15:30,938
So,

1573
01:15:30,982 --> 01:15:33,724
this is the man

1574
01:15:33,767 --> 01:15:36,814
who spent a lifetime
plotting against me.

1575
01:15:38,903 --> 01:15:41,253
I wouldn't have
known your face

1576
01:15:41,296 --> 01:15:44,822
if it had been on a billboard
outside my bedroom window.

1577
01:15:44,865 --> 01:15:47,128
But you have spent,
what, 30 years

1578
01:15:47,172 --> 01:15:48,608
thinking about mine?

1579
01:15:48,652 --> 01:15:50,131
When my father died,

1580
01:15:50,175 --> 01:15:52,133
your insurance company
denied my mother her claims.

1581
01:15:52,177 --> 01:15:53,570
I wouldn't
even have known...She died a pauper!

1582
01:15:53,613 --> 01:15:55,484
...who your mother was.

1583
01:15:55,528 --> 01:15:56,573
She was a digit,

1584
01:15:56,616 --> 01:16:00,141
a nanobyte
in a stream of data.

1585
01:16:00,185 --> 01:16:02,100
Because nothing
is personal to you

1586
01:16:02,143 --> 01:16:04,450
and everyone and everything
is just a number,
isn't that so?

1587
01:16:04,493 --> 01:16:07,148
That is where
you are wrong,
Mr. Rhodes.

1588
01:16:07,192 --> 01:16:12,110
Once you made yourself known
it became very personal.

1589
01:16:13,372 --> 01:16:15,243
My son...Yeah, the sociopath.

1590
01:16:15,287 --> 01:16:16,636
TRESSLER: Funny thing is,

1591
01:16:16,680 --> 01:16:19,987
I have seven so-called
legitimate children.

1592
01:16:20,031 --> 01:16:21,641
Sniveling, snobbish,

1593
01:16:21,685 --> 01:16:23,512
stupid runts.

1594
01:16:23,556 --> 01:16:26,994
I have one illegitimate child
who is a lot like me.

1595
01:16:27,038 --> 01:16:29,475
The point is,
he wants something,

1596
01:16:29,518 --> 01:16:31,085
and like any good parent,

1597
01:16:31,129 --> 01:16:33,610
I will stop at nothing

1598
01:16:33,653 --> 01:16:34,741
to get it for him.

1599
01:16:34,785 --> 01:16:36,613
Your Horsemen have it.

1600
01:16:36,656 --> 01:16:39,006
You will turn it and them

1601
01:16:39,050 --> 01:16:40,965
over to us, now.

1602
01:16:41,008 --> 01:16:42,096
No.

1603
01:16:43,184 --> 01:16:45,796
[GROANING]

1604
01:16:45,839 --> 01:16:48,537
WALTER: Dylan, I would
like you to really
take this moment

1605
01:16:48,581 --> 01:16:50,191
because this is
the consequence

1606
01:16:50,235 --> 01:16:52,150
of your personal
vendetta come to life

1607
01:16:52,193 --> 01:16:54,021
and staring you
in the face.

1608
01:16:54,065 --> 01:16:55,675
I want you to know
that when you're gone,

1609
01:16:55,719 --> 01:16:57,024
we're not going to stop.

1610
01:16:57,068 --> 01:16:59,157
We're gonna destroy
everything you believe in,

1611
01:16:59,200 --> 01:17:01,376
starting with the Horsemen,
and ending with the Eye.

1612
01:17:01,420 --> 01:17:03,291
Now then,
cast your mind back

1613
01:17:03,335 --> 01:17:06,512
to standing by
the banks of the river
watching your father descend,

1614
01:17:06,555 --> 01:17:08,557
disgraced and discredited.

1615
01:17:08,601 --> 01:17:11,386
The horrid psychic pain
as you have relived for years.

1616
01:17:12,083 --> 01:17:14,215
I felt that same thing

1617
01:17:14,259 --> 01:17:15,521
two years ago

1618
01:17:15,564 --> 01:17:17,044
as you drained not
just my father's fortune,

1619
01:17:17,088 --> 01:17:19,133
but his dignity![GROANS]

1620
01:17:19,177 --> 01:17:21,179
And yet you took
pleasure from it.

1621
01:17:24,008 --> 01:17:26,619
This should bring back
some childhood memories.

1622
01:17:35,454 --> 01:17:36,629
[GROANS]

1623
01:17:52,166 --> 01:17:53,951
[POUNDING ON DOOR]

1624
01:17:53,994 --> 01:17:55,909
Would you like
some tea?Oh. Thank you.

1625
01:17:55,953 --> 01:17:56,997
[MUFFLED GRUNTING]

1626
01:18:11,533 --> 01:18:13,797
You ready?Over to you.

1627
01:18:20,847 --> 01:18:21,892
Splash!

1628
01:18:22,370 --> 01:18:23,545
[CHUCKLING]

1629
01:18:25,460 --> 01:18:26,810
Job done!

1630
01:18:42,477 --> 01:18:45,480
TRESSLER: Hell is going
to seem like
a day at the spa

1631
01:18:45,524 --> 01:18:48,440
by the time we're through
with these Horsemen.

1632
01:18:48,483 --> 01:18:51,182
Wouldn't you say?WALTER:
You had me at "hell."

1633
01:18:51,225 --> 01:18:52,705
[MUFFLED SCREAMING]

1634
01:19:08,025 --> 01:19:10,462
[GASPING]LIONEL:  I love you so much.

1635
01:19:10,505 --> 01:19:12,943
[YELLING IN FRUSTRATION]

1636
01:19:12,986 --> 01:19:15,423
Always keep something
up my sleeve.

1637
01:19:15,467 --> 01:19:17,121
[PANTING]

1638
01:20:13,655 --> 01:20:15,048
[CLICKING]

1639
01:20:31,804 --> 01:20:34,241
[SIGHS]

1640
01:20:34,285 --> 01:20:37,375
I wish I could dredge
from the muck of my soul

1641
01:20:37,418 --> 01:20:39,594
one speck of remorse,

1642
01:20:39,638 --> 01:20:41,553
but I can't.

1643
01:20:41,596 --> 01:20:44,904
So I'll stick to
the business at hand

1644
01:20:44,948 --> 01:20:47,298
and try not to smile
too broadly.

1645
01:20:48,081 --> 01:20:50,910
And, uh, thank you

1646
01:20:50,954 --> 01:20:53,391
for delivering
Mr. Dylan Rhodes.

1647
01:20:54,174 --> 01:20:55,915
I take it it's done.

1648
01:20:57,264 --> 01:20:59,223
Literally hit
the bottom.

1649
01:20:59,832 --> 01:21:00,833
Now,

1650
01:21:01,834 --> 01:21:03,531
where are the Horsemen?

1651
01:21:03,575 --> 01:21:05,533
They're performers.

1652
01:21:05,577 --> 01:21:07,884
Their pride, their ego...

1653
01:21:07,927 --> 01:21:11,191
Their need to be adored
are all too powerful

1654
01:21:11,235 --> 01:21:13,106
to keep them out of
the limelight for long.

1655
01:21:13,150 --> 01:21:16,370
If they don't make
themselves known,

1656
01:21:16,414 --> 01:21:18,764
you will find yourself

1657
01:21:18,807 --> 01:21:21,114
in a very similar position

1658
01:21:21,158 --> 01:21:22,811
to Mr. Rhodes.

1659
01:21:22,855 --> 01:21:24,596
Are we clear about that?

1660
01:21:24,639 --> 01:21:26,685
As clear as the water
he's under.

1661
01:21:34,171 --> 01:21:35,955
You'll have the rest

1662
01:21:35,999 --> 01:21:37,739
when I have the Horsemen.

1663
01:22:09,989 --> 01:22:11,034
ALL: Dylan!

1664
01:22:12,470 --> 01:22:14,863
JACK: Dylan, come on,
buddy, breathe!

1665
01:22:14,907 --> 01:22:16,169
MERRITT: Dylan.LULA: Dylan?

1666
01:22:16,213 --> 01:22:18,302
MERRITT: Dylan, come on![COUGHING]

1667
01:22:19,738 --> 01:22:21,392
[DYLAN PANTING]

1668
01:22:22,567 --> 01:22:25,309
You're okay.[SIGHING]

1669
01:22:25,352 --> 01:22:28,094
Jesus! You scared
the hell out of us, man.

1670
01:22:28,138 --> 01:22:29,313
Are you all right, bro?

1671
01:22:29,748 --> 01:22:31,880
Okay!

1672
01:22:31,924 --> 01:22:33,882
Thank you!This is the least
I could do.

1673
01:22:33,926 --> 01:22:35,884
No. There's a hell of a lot
less you could've done.

1674
01:22:35,928 --> 01:22:37,234
That was not an option.

1675
01:22:37,277 --> 01:22:39,192
You took a bullet
for us, it was huge.

1676
01:22:39,236 --> 01:22:40,541
You really did, man.

1677
01:22:43,936 --> 01:22:45,590
Thanks for
pulling me out.
Seriously.

1678
01:22:46,547 --> 01:22:47,940
[SOFTLY] Yeah.

1679
01:22:47,984 --> 01:22:50,116
LULA: You got yourself out.
We did the easy part.

1680
01:22:50,160 --> 01:22:51,900
Literally, in my case,

1681
01:22:51,944 --> 01:22:53,119
I was just standing
on the shore while
Atlas jumped down

1682
01:22:53,163 --> 01:22:54,207
and got you.[CHUCKLING]

1683
01:22:54,251 --> 01:22:55,992
I'm serious.

1684
01:22:56,035 --> 01:22:57,906
Hey, you guys.
Something's not right.

1685
01:22:57,950 --> 01:22:59,169
What's wrong?LULA: What?

1686
01:23:01,258 --> 01:23:02,346
It's fake.

1687
01:23:02,389 --> 01:23:03,608
LULA: What?

1688
01:23:05,305 --> 01:23:06,915
LULA: No, I had the stick.

1689
01:23:06,959 --> 01:23:09,048
The actual stick.
I swear, it was in my hand.

1690
01:23:09,092 --> 01:23:11,572
In the lab.
And then I put it in
the little case thing.

1691
01:23:11,616 --> 01:23:12,791
And I gave it to Atlas.

1692
01:23:12,834 --> 01:23:14,532
Right, which I then
gave to Dylan.

1693
01:23:14,575 --> 01:23:16,751
Is there any
chance you've possibly
misplaced it at any point?

1694
01:23:16,795 --> 01:23:18,275
No.

1695
01:23:18,318 --> 01:23:20,799
I took it from you
and then slipped it
back in your coat

1696
01:23:20,842 --> 01:23:22,757
when I pushed you out.

1697
01:23:22,801 --> 01:23:25,586
Either way, we're
left holding a whole
sack full of nada.

1698
01:23:25,630 --> 01:23:28,241
Yeah, but they're gonna
come after us as if
we do have something.

1699
01:23:28,285 --> 01:23:30,591
No. Okay.
I agree that somebody
got the better of us.

1700
01:23:30,635 --> 01:23:32,028
Okay? Somehow.

1701
01:23:32,071 --> 01:23:34,204
But I don't agree
that we have a sack
full of nada.

1702
01:23:34,247 --> 01:23:35,466
Because we're all here.

1703
01:23:35,509 --> 01:23:37,424
That's a sack
full of something.

1704
01:23:38,425 --> 01:23:40,297
Listen.

1705
01:23:40,340 --> 01:23:45,128
We all know that Walter
is not going to stop
until he gets that chip.

1706
01:23:45,171 --> 01:23:48,783
And we're the only ones that
even know that he's alive.

1707
01:23:48,827 --> 01:23:51,438
We can't just walk away.

1708
01:23:51,482 --> 01:23:53,440
That's not what
the Horsemen do.

1709
01:23:56,182 --> 01:23:58,097
There's a quote. Um...

1710
01:23:58,141 --> 01:23:59,577
It's actually
by the magician

1711
01:23:59,620 --> 01:24:01,318
that made me wanna do this
in the first place.

1712
01:24:01,361 --> 01:24:03,320
It's, uh...

1713
01:24:03,363 --> 01:24:07,759
"A magician's greatest power
lies forever shrouded

1714
01:24:07,802 --> 01:24:10,109
"in his empty fist."

1715
01:24:10,153 --> 01:24:12,503
"And the very idea
that he can convince
the world

1716
01:24:12,546 --> 01:24:15,723
"that he is, in fact,
carrying with him a secret."

1717
01:24:15,767 --> 01:24:17,290
That's Lionel Shrike.

1718
01:24:17,334 --> 01:24:18,335
Right.

1719
01:24:19,901 --> 01:24:21,425
JACK: So what are you saying?

1720
01:24:21,468 --> 01:24:23,688
That we should pretend like
